<meta type=article>
  <title | Table test fixture>
  <author | Ariel Balter>
</meta>

<section | Inline CSV>

A numbered table with caption from inline CSV:

<table #tab:csv csv caption="Greek letters and values" | key,value,notes
alpha,1,First entry
beta,2,Second entry
gamma,3,"Quoted, third"
>

<section | TSV>

A TSV table without headers:

<table #tab:tsv tsv -headers | col1	col2	col3
A	B	C
D	E	F
>

<section | JSON>

A JSON table from an array of objects:

<table #tab:json json caption="Coordinates" | [{"x": 1, "y": 2}, {"x": 3, "y": 4}]>

<section | YAML>

A YAML table from a sequence of mappings:

<table #tab:yaml yaml caption="YAML data" | - name: Alice
  score: 95
- name: Bob
  score: 87
>

<section | Markdown pipe table>

<table #tab:md md caption="Pipe table" | | Symbol | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| F      | Force   |
| m      | Mass    |
| a      | Acceleration |
>

<section | Cross-references>

See <ref #tab:csv> for the CSV table,
<ref #tab:json> for JSON,
and <ref #tab:md> for the markdown pipe table.

<section | File source>

A table loaded from an external CSV file:

<table #tab:src csv src=sample-data.csv caption="From file" | >

<section | Unnumbered table>

<table #tab:unnumbered csv -numbered caption="Unnumbered" | a,b
1,2
>

An unnumbered table does not appear in the numbered sequence. See <ref #tab:unnumbered>.
